VeridianOS: powerdevil: moc for the ddcutil detector only with ddcutil

daemon/controllers/ddcutildetector.cpp declares its QObject
(DDCutilPrivateSingleton) inside #ifdef WITH_DDCUTIL, but includes
"ddcutildetector.moc" whatever the configuration. AutoMoc does not
evaluate #ifdef, so a build without ddcutil (as here) ran moc on the
file for nothing: "ddcutildetector.cpp: note: No relevant classes found.
No output generated." Without ddcutil the source is now left to AutoMoc
(SKIP_AUTOMOC) and its two moc includes are compiled only with ddcutil;
the header's QObject (DDCutilDetector) is then compiled through AutoMoc's
mocs_compilation.cpp, as for any header no source includes the output
of. With ddcutil nothing changes.

--- a/daemon/controllers/ddcutildetector.cpp
+++ b/daemon/controllers/ddcutildetector.cpp
@@ -291,5 +291,9 @@
     return result;
 }
 
+// Only with ddcutil: without it the file declares nothing for moc and is
+// left to AutoMoc (daemon/CMakeLists.txt).
+#ifdef WITH_DDCUTIL
 #include "ddcutildetector.moc"
 #include "moc_ddcutildetector.cpp"
+#endif
--- a/daemon/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/daemon/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -4,6 +4,12 @@
                     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR})
 
 add_subdirectory(actions)
+
+# ddcutildetector.cpp has a QObject only with ddcutil (WITH_DDCUTIL); its
+# header's moc output is compiled through mocs_compilation.cpp without it.
+if(NOT DDCUtil_FOUND)
+    set_source_files_properties(controllers/ddcutildetector.cpp PROPERTIES SKIP_AUTOMOC ON)
+endif()
 
 # target no.1 - powerdevil core library
 set(powerdevilcore_SRCS
